Subject: [PATCH] Redesign homepage: full-width TopNav + live member dashboard
 hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Matches the provided reference design:
- TopNav rebuilt from a floating pill into a full-width bar: logo +
  wordmark, icon nav items (Home/Learn/E-Book/Routine/Admin), a
  decorative search box, a notification bell, and an avatar dropdown
  (initials + display name derived from email + role + sign out) —
  replaces the old bare logout icon.
- New BoardsOverviewPanel component: the 'All Boards' / 'Recent
  Activity' two-column card on the homepage hero, wired to real data —
  top-level published boards with live class counts, and the 4 most
  recently added classes as the activity feed (videos.created_at),
  each with a 4-color icon cycle matching the reference.
- Homepage stats bar (previously always '—' placeholders) now shows
  real counts: active members, classes published, instructors (mapped
  to the ADMIN role — no separate instructor concept in the schema,
  noted inline), and top-level published board count.
- 'What's inside' section copy/cards replaced to match the reference
  (Structured Boards / Focused Classes / Private by Design / Fast &
  Simple) with icons instead of the old placeholder gradient boxes.
- Hero layout branches on auth: signed-in members get the two-column
  dashboard hero with the live boards panel (guests never see real
  board/video data, consistent with boards' RLS policy); logged-out
  visitors keep the original centered marketing hero.
- All new Supabase reads are counts or already-published-only content,
  through the same admin-client-for-videos/authorized_users pattern
  used elsewhere in the app for tables with no regular-user RLS policy.

tsc --noEmit is clean; a full `next build` got past compilation and
failed only on the sandbox's lack of internet access to Google Fonts,
which will resolve normally on Vercel.
